s":"2026-10-25T12:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Uncompahgre Plateau/Dallas Divide; Northwestern San Juan Mountains; Southwest San Juan Mountains; Paradox Valley/Lower Dolores River; Four Corners/Upper Dolores River; Animas River Basin; San Juan River Basin; Southeast Utah; Arches/Grand Flat; La Sal and Abajo Mountains; Canyonlands/Natural Bridges","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a28b19253bb7550e7a42b701dae47ec9af4c8ee0.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a28b19253bb7550e7a42b701dae47ec9af4c8ee0.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued October 23 at 11:33AM MDT until October 23 at 1:45PM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues.\n\n* WHERE...West Central Montezuma County in southwestern Colorado...\nSoutheastern San Juan County in southeastern Utah along the San\nJuan River from the Four Corners to Lake Powell...\n\n* WHEN...Until 145 PM MDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of rivers, creeks, streams, and other low-lying\nand flood-prone locations is occurring. The San Juan River will\ncontinue to rise this afternoon through Bluff and Mexican Hat.\nProjected peak will occur around midnight tonight.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 1130 AM MDT, River forecasts estimate a peak on the San Juan\nRiver near Bluff to exceed 25 feet tonight, with a secondary peak\nexpected overnight Saturday into Sunday. Gauge reports indicated\nhigh accumulations of rainfall since Thursday. Flooding is\nongoing in the warned area.\n- This includes the following streams and drainages...\nTohache Wash, San Juan River, Toh Dahstini Wash and Cowboy Wash.\nFlooding impacts will continue, but no additional rainfall is\nexpected.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nMexican Hat, Tselakai Dezza, Bluff, Halchita, Montezuma Creek and\nAneth.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-23T13:45:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Montezuma, CO; San Juan, UT","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.72a7423d11769ccf8f839bc6361c28f222c31fb9.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.72a7423d11769ccf8f839bc6361c28f222c31fb9.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued October 23 at 10:31AM MDT until October 23 at 12:45PM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"* WHAT...Small stream flooding caused by excessive rainfall\ncontinues.\n\n* WHERE...West Central Montezuma County in southwestern Colorado...\nSoutheastern San Juan County in southeastern Utah...\n\n* WHEN...Until 1245 PM MDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of rivers, creeks, streams, and other low-lying\nand flood-prone locations is occurring.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 1031 AM MDT, gauge reports indicated heavy rain accumulations\nsince Thursday. Flooding is ongoing in the warned area. Between\n1.2 and 2 inches of rain have fallen.\n- Flooding impacts will continue, but no additional rainfall is\nexpected.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nCortez and Aneth.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-23T12:45:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Montezuma, CO; San Juan, UT","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.c5e08ea6585686cf32784f047437454d3595a5f5.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.c5e08ea6585686cf32784f047437454d3595a5f5.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Advisory","headline":"Flood Advisory issued October 23 at 1:51AM MDT until October 23 at 1:45PM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...Northeastern Montezuma County in southwestern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 145 PM MDT Friday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 150 AM MDT, Gauge reports indicated heavy rain due to\nthunderstorms. Minor flooding is ongoing or expected to begin\nshortly in the advisory area.\n- This includes the following streams and dra